cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BanglaChhanda: a rule-based scanner and pilot corpus for Bangla verse"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Morol
    given-names: Md Kishor
    alias: kishormorol
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4468-8260"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kishormorol/banglachhanda"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/kishormorol/banglachhanda"
abstract: >-
  A rule-based scanner for Bangla verse and a pilot corpus for chhanda
  annotation. The scanner derives syllable structure, matra counts and foot
  divisions under akkharbritta, matrabritta and svarabritta, flagging the cases
  where the rules are genuinely uncertain rather than guessing. The corpus is 81
  public-domain Tagore poems from Bengali Wikisource with per-poem provenance,
  and a 303-line pilot of pre-filled annotation records. The pilot's labels are
  machine-produced and have not been checked by a human.
keywords:
  - Bangla
  - Bengali
  - prosody
  - scansion
  - meter
  - poetry
  - computational literary studies
